{
  "world_updates": [
    {
      "type": "NPC_SPOKE"
    }
  ],
  "memory_summary": "The Parent continues describing Murky Water, emphasizing its quiet nature and what it hides.",
  "new_entities": [],
  "rule_flags": [],
  "narration": "The Parent settles deeper into the bank of the water, one hand resting on the mud, and speaks slowly, as if the answer is long and the listener is worth the time.",
  "npc_response": "This place is older than the trees. It was here before the river found its way, and it remembers what the land has forgotten. The water does not rush because it has no hurry, only patience. It holds the shape of every footstep that has ever stood here, and it keeps them even after the walker is gone. I come here not to find answers, but to be near something that does not ask me questions. You are new to this, are you not? Then you will understand: the quiet is not empty. It is full of things that do not want to be seen. And that is the kindest thing this water has ever done to me."
}

