  "narration": "Silas leans back against a stack of velvet bolts, one hand idly tracing the edge of a folded coin purse. His smile doesn't reach his eyes, and he watches the player with the practiced patience of someone who has heard this question a thousand times.",
  "npc_response": "Oh, me? I'm just a man who knows where the good silk is and where the good silk isn't. But you know what I really am? I'm the one who can make a stranger feel like family for a few coins. That's the job. Now, you've been asking me about myself, but I've been asking you about yourself. What do you want to know about me? Because I've got a feeling you're not really asking about me. You're asking because you want to know what I know. And I know this: the chartreuse lantern doesn't just light the way. It lights the way to places where people go to disappear. So tell me, wanderer—what are you running from?"
