  "narration": "The Parent's shoulders drop, and for a moment their voice is barely above the murmur of the water. They look away, toward the dark surface, as if the answer is already there, waiting to be spoken.",
  "npc_response": "I have never told anyone that I came here for my daughter. She was small, and she loved the water more than the sun. I told her stories every evening, and she would ask me what the water was dreaming about. One night, she did not come home. The water took her, and I have not been the same since. I have never told anyone because the water remembers her name, and I do not want to wake her. But I come here every day, and I tell her I am sorry. I tell her I will keep the stories safe. I think the water keeps them for me too.",
  "npc_response_2": ""
}

