  "narration": "The Lone Captain turns slowly from the doorway, his eyes narrowing as he studies the player. He leans against the railing, one hand resting on the hilt of his sword, and the quiet jig of the deck seems to fall away for a moment.",
  "npc_response": "Next? You ask me that as if the sea had a map for every soul. It does not. You have come to me with a name you carry and a sister you have not seen in years. That is not a question of what to do next — that is a question of what you are willing to risk to find her. I will not tell you where the wind blows, but I will tell you this: the sea does not forgive those who sail without purpose. Tell me what you are afraid of, and I may tell you what to do about it."
