  "narration": "Silas smooths his worn coat and leans back on the edge of a crate, his eyes glinting with practiced charm. He gestures vaguely at the crowd around him, as if the market itself were his confidant.",
  "npc_response": "Ah, you want to know about me? Stranger, you should be careful what you ask of a man like me. I've been in this market longer than the awnings have held up. I've sold things I'd rather forget, bought things I never should've touched, and learned to read a crowd the way some read a book. But here's the truth I can tell you: I don't trust anyone who asks too many questions. You've already asked me for secrets, and I've given you none. That's because I know what happens to people who know too much. So consider this my story — and if you're going to take it, take it with a grain of salt. The market's full of salt."
}

